      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityofrandolphmn.com/copy-of-about",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Randolph Area Historical Society, founded in 2000, now houses a 2,000‑square‑foot, energy‑efficient museum that preserves the town’s rich history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.rahsmn.org/museum",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1858 Randolph briefly carried the name Richmond before switching to Randolph, likely honoring Virginia statesman John Randolph.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityofrandolphmn.com/copy-of-about",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "John Richmond, the town’s first settler, arrived in the Randolph area in May 1854, laying the groundwork for its future.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityofrandolphmn.com/copy-of-about",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Randolph’s post office has been operating continuously since 1886, a testament to the town’s enduring community.",
